  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multistakeholder Forest Governance and Accountability Project Phase 2 (MFGAP2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MFGAP2 aims to support governance and market reforms that reduce the illegal use of forest resources, while also contributing to improved forest management for poverty reduction, biodiversity conservation, and climate protection. To achieve these goals, MFGAP2 works with a wide variety of stakeholders, including government actors, civil society, and private sector representatives. Through advocacy and engagement, MFGAP2 seeks to strengthen the capacity, transparency, and accountability of local institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
